summary: CUSE acceptance in a fresh KVM guest
description: |
    Run by scripts/cuse-guest.sh, which verifies the pinned cloud image,
    provisions a fresh guest on a throw-away overlay through the user's
    libvirt session, places the selected packages in the plan's data
    directory and destroys the guest afterwards. The guest supplies its own
    kernel, CUSE, udev, systemd and enforcing SELinux policy.

    The image, memory and processors are chosen by the script from the
    target, so that the image, this plan's distro context and the packages
    always agree. Memory and processors come from tmt context; to run the
    plan by hand during development, pass for example
    `-c distro=fedora-43 -c guest_memory_mib=2048 -c guest_cpus=2`.
discover:
    how: fmf
    filter: 'tag:cuse'
provision:
    how: virtual
    connection: session
    hardware:
        memory: $@{guest_memory_mib} MB
        cpu:
            processors: $@{guest_cpus}
execute:
    how: tmt
